hl for Debian
-------------

This package ships no configuration file, deliberately.

hl looks for configuration in two places: your own directory
(~/.config/hl/) and a system-wide one (/etc/hl/). It has a complete set of
defaults compiled into the binary, so it works with neither present.

Shipping a copy of those defaults into /etc/hl/ would make it a dpkg conffile:
tracked, and prompted about on every upgrade that changes it, in exchange for a
file that only restates what the binary already does. So the defaults are
shipped as an example instead.

To customise, copy it and edit your copy:

  /usr/share/doc/hl/examples/config.toml  ->  ~/.config/hl/config.toml

or, for every user on the machine, to /etc/hl/config.toml. A file you create
there is yours: dpkg does not own it and will not touch it.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>
